index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8ff0314a11e1ed65dd822dd0d4cd89e80e50b0c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,185 @@
+# Critical maximum independent sets (arXiv:0906.4609)
+
+> Status: the generator passes every local gate, but it is **not yet shippable**.
+> The required OpenRouter runs were attempted twice and every request was refused
+> with HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`; no model received the problem.  G9 and the
+> bare hardening verdict therefore remain pending, not failed.
+
+| Profile field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite discrete |
+| Computational core | graph |
+| Certificate form | integer tuple (a vertex set) |
+| Intended intuition | constraint propagation from equality in a matching bound |
+| Domain essentiality | native |
+| Reduction | none |
+
+## What the family is
+
+The source is Levit and Mandrescu, [*Critical independent sets and
+König–Egerváry graphs*](https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.4609).  An instance gives a
+finite simple graph and a matching with one exposed vertex.  The solver returns
+an independent set containing 97 vertices: the exposed vertex and one endpoint
+from each of 96 matching edges.
+
+This is a fully local witness.  A matching edge contributes at most one vertex
+to an independent set, so a set of size `|M|+1` is maximum.  Mapping every
+selected matched endpoint to its mate injects the covered part of any independent
+set into its neighborhood, proving `|S|-|N(S)| <= 1`; the returned set attains
+one.  `verify` checks the matching, independence, neighborhood, and all
+cardinalities exactly without reading `inst["answer"]`.
+
+Generation is inverse.  It samples one endpoint from every matching pair, adds
+the exposed vertex, and only then adds edges that avoid this set.  Dense
+constraint blocks and complementary-side edges are added after the certificate
+exists.  The matching and the planted set prove `alpha(G)+mu(G)=|V|` by
+construction, so the graph is König–Egerváry; Theorem 2.7 says every maximum
+independent set is critical.
+
+## Why this is Track B
+
+Track A would be false.  Section 1 explicitly records that critical independent
+sets are polynomial-time computable, and Theorem 2.7 identifies the maximum
+critical set with a maximum independent set on these graphs.  The supplied
+matching gives an even sharper algorithm: choosing one endpoint per edge turns
+every graph edge into a 2-SAT clause, solved by implication-graph strongly
+connected components in `O(|V|+|E|)`.
+
+At shipping `n=96`, seed 271828, the SCC reference used 5,373 implication-arc
+constructions/DFS scans and about 0.0009 seconds; it solves 8/8 audited seeds, as
+expected.  The compact route notices that tightness forces the exposed vertex,
+then propagates matching orientations through alternating reachability.  It
+orients each of the 96 matching edges once.  The implementation also read 797
+adjacency entries on the measured shipping seed, which is an important practical
+caveat even though no exact arithmetic is involved.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+`make_instance(seed=0, n=6, block_size=3, cross_percent=70,
+internal_percent=15)` renders as:
+
+```text
+Find a critical maximum independent set in a finite graph.
+
+Vertices: 0 through 12.  Required set size: 7.
+Matching: (4,8) (2,1) (12,11) (7,9) (3,10) (5,6)
+
+Adjacency:
+  0: 11
+  1: 2 3 5 6
+  2: 1 6
+  3: 1 10
+  4: 8 9 11
+  5: 1 6 10
+  6: 1 2 5 7 10
+  7: 6 9 11
+  8: 4 11 12
+  9: 4 7 12
+  10: 3 5 6
+  11: 0 4 7 8 12
+  12: 8 9 11
+
+Return 7 distinct labels in increasing order as a JSON list inside
+<answer></answer> tags.
+```
+
+The full renderer additionally defines independence, open neighborhood,
+critical difference, indexing, ordering, and the matching bound.  The answer is
+`[0,2,3,4,5,7,12]`.  The demo is hand-solvable: vertex 0 is the sole exposed
+vertex, so 11 is excluded; matching tightness and adjacency propagate the six
+remaining choices.
+
+```python
+>>> verify(inst, [0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 12])
+(True, 'ok')
+>>> verify(inst, [0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7])
+(False, 'wrong length: expected 7 vertices')
+```
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| Preset | Matching pairs | Block size | Cross % | Internal % | Status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 6 | 3 | 70 | 15 | hand example; never ships |
+| easy | 96 | 16 | 50 | 15 | provisional shipping level; oracle run blocked |
+| medium | 112 | 14 | 50 | 15 | available, not reached |
+| hard | 128 | 16 | 50 | 15 | available, not reached |
+
+No preset has been rejected.  `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY="easy"` is provisional until
+the bare and hinted oracle runs produce `hardened` verdicts.
+
+## Gate results
+
+| Gate | Result | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 witnesses, all presets and three seeds; JSON round-trip |
+| G2 | pass | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged JSON recovered through prose and a Markdown fence |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; language size `2^96` |
+| G5 | pass | shipping density 0/200,000; exact density `1/2^96`; demo count 1/64; reference cost 5,373 operations |
+| G6 | pass | four attacks each 0/8; SCC reference 8/8; compact closure 8/8 |
+| G7 | pass | doubled `n=192` builds and verifies; answer-space exponent doubles |
+| G8 | pass | 140/140 relabelling compositions invariant and real; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9 | **pending** | local caps pass: 329 chars, 97 atoms, 96 orientation operations; oracle arms unavailable |
+
+The four failing G6 attacks are lower-degree endpoint selection, static greedy
+matching order, 256 random orientation restarts, and the in-context heuristic
+that performs only one propagation hop from the exposed vertex.  All are 0/8.
+The reference SCC solver used 41,844 recorded operations across those eight
+instances.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+| Run | Preset | Calls answered | Result |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| bare, default 32k ceiling | easy | 0 | aborted after four HTTP 403 quota errors |
+| bare, diagnostic 12k ceiling | easy | 0 | aborted after four HTTP 403 quota errors; this transcript is preserved |
+| structural hint | — | 0 | not run because the same key is quota-blocked |
+| placebo hint | — | 0 | not run because the same key is quota-blocked |
+
+There is no hinted-minus-placebo estimate and no hinted verdict.  The structural
+hint names only the alternating-reachability invariant; it does not give a
+procedure or a derived count.  When access is restored, rerun the bare loop in
+this directory and the hinted/placebo loops in separate scratch directories, as
+required by the harness.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_0906_4609 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, parse_answer, render, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=12345, **DIFFICULTY["easy"])
+question = render(inst)
+candidate = parse_answer("<answer>[0,2,5]</answer>")
+ok, reason = verify(inst, candidate)
+```
+
+After all oracle gates pass, emit from the repository root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 0906.4609 20 easy
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+- This is emphatically Track B.  The included SCC implementation solves every
+  audited instance in under a millisecond; the family makes no complexity-theoretic
+  hardness claim.
+- G4 samples the exact prior a reader gets for free from the displayed matching:
+  the exposed vertex plus one uniformly random endpoint per edge.  Its `1/2^96`
+  density says nothing about correlated propagation or spectral heuristics.
+- The compact route performs only 96 forced orientations but reads about 750–800
+  adjacency entries.  A failure can therefore reflect bookkeeping as well as
+  discovery of the invariant; the G9 arms are needed to measure that distinction.
+- A full spectral relaxation, SAT package, and generic maximum-critical-independent-set
+  implementation were not counted as failing attacks.  They are expected to
+  succeed; the exact 2-SAT SCC solver is the stronger relevant reference here.
+- `canonical_key` is a typed 1-dimensional Weisfeiler–Leman fingerprint, not a
+  complete graph-isomorphism canonical form.  It is proven only for arbitrary
+  vertex relabelling, edge reordering, matching reordering, and all their
+  compositions, plus empirical separation of 20 unrelated instances.
+- The only present blocker is external quota.  The four 403 records in
+  `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl` are infrastructure errors, not evidence that an
+  oracle failed the mathematical problem.
