The family is honestly declared Track B because critical-independent-set search is polynomial, as the paper itself notes; Theorem 2.7 supplies the criticality characterization. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/0906.4609v2), [polynomial critical-set algorithm](https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/0403037).

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Guessing: 0/200,000 from the structure-aware \(2^{96}\) space.
- Four heuristic attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference 2-SAT algorithm: 8/8, about 5,373 operations per shipping instance.
- Canonical-key tests: 300/300 invariance checks and 20/20 distinct unrelated instances.

The oracle run found `easy`, `medium`, `hard`, and the first escalation too easy. During the next escalation, OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” and the harness could not finish. The isolated G9 runs encountered the same quota block. Consequently, no hardness verdict was claimed and no `REJECTED.md` was written. Restoring the OpenRouter quota and rerunning `harden.py` is required to finish.
